1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,240
What if it never stopped getting quieter?

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:05,000
It's getting quieter.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,440
A normal conversation is about 60 decibels.

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,520
The traffic fades away.

5
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:13,800
A quiet library: about 40 decibels.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,960
The birds stop singing.

7
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,760
A whisper is about 30 decibels.

8
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:20,920
Even the wind goes still.

9
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,960
Rustling leaves: about 20 decibels.

10
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,440
Now you can hear yourself breathe.

11
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:29,080
Normal breathing is about 10 decibels.

12
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,080
Then, nothing at all.

13
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:35,560
0 decibels is the quietest sound a healthy human ear can detect.

14
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:37,400
But you still hear something.

15
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:44,120
In one famous study, 94% of people in a soundproof room started hearing ringing that wasn't there.

16
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,360
Your heartbeat. Your blood.

17
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:53,720
The quietest room ever measured: about −20 decibels. People inside can hear their own hearts beating.

18
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,720
Then even that is gone.

19
00:00:55,720 --> 00:01:02,040
At about −23 decibels, the only sound left would be air molecules hitting your eardrums.

20
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,640
Total silence.

21
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,720
So you would hear anything.

22
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,780
Even something breathing…

23
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,410
right behind you.

24
00:01:11,232 --> 00:01:13,252
Wait.

25
00:01:13,752 --> 00:01:16,852
What if it never stopped getting closer?

26
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:21,250
What if it never stopped getting quieter?
